  "mechanisms": {
    "creation": "xxxLBCreate derives original style flags, creates string storage, measures font and sends original WM_MEASUREITEM; fallback dimensions use current invocation metrics. Native GetThreadLocale/GetDC/ReleaseDC, heap and GDI are not F ownership. GdiGetCharDimensions maps to B wow_native_controls (C0393 already eliminated).",
    "destruction": "Original xxxDestroyLBox sends owner-draw delete notifications before freeing item/string/tab/search storage; then FreeLookasideEntry, FNID_CLEANEDUP_BIT and original combo WM_PARENTNOTIFY. FreeLookasideEntry resolves C rtlinit; ListboxLookaside source definition and initialization are C lb1.c. The map common label alone does not establish ownership.",
    "fnid": "F wow_edit_set_window_fnid derives original ntstubs NtUserSetWindowFNID, validates current retained window then applies original FNID/CLEANEDUP logic. It consumes private C layout through F window identity. Keep lifecycle state ownership coherent in S13; original subset choice remains S14, not an unapproved whole-file mirror reimport.",
    "resize": "Original xxxLBSize expects SetWindowPos-triggered recursive resize and returns immediately after the call. GetWindowBorders resolves C rtl/winmgr.c; CopyInflateRect resolves B wow_control_rect. Shared edit entry captures geometry context before original call, restores prior context in finally. MoveWindow/SetWindowPos/InvalidateRect/SendMessage use F native-call boundary; retain synchronous/reentrant semantics when removing outward dependency.",
    "variableHeight": "lboxvar stores byte item heights after item/selection arrays, computes pages and visible-item bounds using C helpers. Empty-list height reads gpsi->cySysFontChar. This maps to F TLS wow_edit_current, owned by shared edit_entry; a new global cache would introduce a second state owner. S13 must untangle metric representation and invocation ownership together.",
    "method": "Both complete source files read; actual COFF undefined lists, VALID Ninja dependencies, link map and source edges checked. No runtime verification claim; classification does not prove adapter minimality."
